        className: "tp-qa-answer",
        children: ["\n", (0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.p, {
          children: "The three major NLP conferences are ACL, EMNLP, and NAACL. ACL (Association for Computational Linguistics) is the flagship and oldest NLP conference, founded in 1962. It covers all areas of computational linguistics and NLP, has a 22-25% acceptance rate, and is held annually in the summer. EMNLP (Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing) focuses on empirical, data-driven NLP research, has a slightly lower acceptance rate (~20-25%), and is held in the fall (Nov-Dec). EMNLP places strong emphasis on reproducibility and large-scale experiments. It sometimes surpasses ACL in submission volume. NAACL (North American Chapter of ACL) serves the North American NLP community with similar scope to ACL, held in the spring. In some years, NAACL replaces the annual ACL meeting for North America. All three conferences host shared tasks — standardized evaluation campaigns on tasks like machine translation, summarization, and question answering. The ACL Anthology (aclanthology.org) archives all papers from all three conferences."
        }), "\n  "]
